{
  "_about": "Geometry of the big set window of the Scapes style (5 x 2 slots), the single source the editor reads to lay a set over the window templates in this folder. Units: pixels of the template images (all four share one geometry and one size); x, y is the top-left corner. The images are the game window cropped to its outline and scaled by 0.8, so a 430 x 480 card is drawn at 344 x 384. Draw order: card images at slots[].card, then the template on top (its picture openings are transparent and its frame covers the card edges), then the texts. Text boxes are where lettering goes: height = the measured height of the original capitals with their outline, width = the free space; centre the text in the box and shrink it to fit the width. color = letter fill, stroke = letter outline; outlines that change with the window colour are in templates.<colour>. The plaque under each card is part of the template; the window colour labels are the style bible's names.",
